%PDF-1.7
%‚„œ”
% AnnotationFallbackTest.pdf - graphical unit tests for annotation fallback rendering.
%
% Rules
% - One page per annotation type, then one page per shared feature.
% - Only features the library supports. Broken input the library handles is a feature too.
% - One case per feature. Every annotation has Contents saying what it tests and what is expected.
%   FreeText and Line captions draw their Contents, so there the drawn text is the description.
% - No annotation has an appearance stream, except the Invisible control cases on the Flags page and
%   the H Invert appearance case on the Link page.
% - Pages are 840 x 840. Grid: 8 x 8 cells of 100 x 100, no gaps, 20 margins.
%   Cell (column c, row r), row 0 at the top: left = 20 + 100c, top = 820 - 100r.
%   A case may span several cells; it never leaves its cells.
% - The page content draws the cell outlines in light gray, plus text or backgrounds a case needs underneath.
% - Each page lists its cases in reading order: standard cases first (defaults, C, IC, border width,
%   dashed, CA), then the cases specific to the type.
% - Contents always start with the annotation subtype, e.g. "Link: ...".
% - Pages:
%    1. Text
%    2. FreeText
%    3. Line
%    4. Square
%    5. Circle
%    6. Polygon
%    7. PolyLine
%    8. Ink
%    9. Highlight
%   10. Underline
%   11. Squiggly
%   12. StrikeOut
%   13. Stamp
%   14. Caret
%   15. FileAttachment
%   16. Link
%   17. Line endings
%   18. Border effects
%   19. Border style
%   20. Color and opacity
%   21. Flags
% - Not covered until supported: Redact, Widget, Beveled and
%   Inset border styles, underline border on FreeText, cloudy PolyLine, FreeText DS and rich text,
%   Text State, Measure, StampImage and StampSnapshot appearances (they exist
%   only as an appearance stream).
%   Out of scope: Sound, Movie, Screen, PrinterMark, TrapNet, Watermark, 3D, RichMedia, Projection.
% - Edit by hand. The xref is a stub with a bogus startxref: readers repair it by scanning the objects,
%   so no offsets need maintaining. Keep /Root in the trailer pointing at the catalog.
1 0 obj
<< /Type /Font /Subtype /Type1 /BaseFont /Helvetica /Encoding /WinAnsiEncoding >>
endobj

